From u8aa9b8cc06fdc99c at groups.google.com  Tue Apr  9 21:47:17 2013
From: u8aa9b8cc06fdc99c at groups.google.com (Bob Carpenter)
Date: Tue, 09 Apr 2013 21:47:17 +0000
Subject: | is not a synonym for ||
Message-ID: <mHCmAoX0Ohw.Mx1GdJgW0K4J@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-dev/c/mHCmAoX0Ohw/m/Mx1GdJgW0K4J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The single vbar (|) is for bitwise or.

The double vbar (||) is for logical or.

There are two reasons to use the logical-or operation
for logical operations:

  1.  it's clearer what the intent is, and

  2.  it works by short circuiting, so if the first
      disjunct is true, the whole thing evaluates to true
      without considering the other disjuncts.

- Bob

