Nope - iostreams are literally streams and don't implement the functionality required for carriage return (which would require more integration into the terminal environment).  \r works on Windows and some Linux boxes but it's not guaranteed.  It looks like ncurses is the only library that enables carriage-return functionality on most systems, but it also does so with significantly more overhead than iostreams.

