>      >     the index type directly, which would let us just standardize
>      >     on size_t for indexing everything.
>      >
>      >
>      > It has been configurable for dense matrices since 3.0. But the Eigen people had a long discussion about this and
>     decided
>      > that signed types were better, mostly due to avoiding bugs in loops. I don't think there are too many cases in
>      > statistical modeling where one wants a matrix whose rows or columns is more than a signed integer can hold. So,
