Be sure to initialize the covariance matrix in the dense_metro constructor,

      dense_metro(M& m,

                  BaseRNG& rng,
                  std::ostream* error_msg)

        : base_metro<M, BaseRNG>(m, rng, error_msg),
          _prop_covar(Eigen::MatrixXd::Identity(m.num_params_r(), m.num_params_r()) {
        this->_name = "Metropolis with a dense Euclidean metric";
        this->_nom_epsilon = 1;
      }

You don't need to mess with _prop_covar in the adapt_dense_metro constructor.

Eventually we should gives users the option to input their own covariance matrix, but I think that's more appropriate as a seed or some function that reads in a file and builds the matrix.  In any case, let's get the basic version working first.

